==Overview==
<tabber>
|-|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Large hitboxes.
* Decent mobility.
* Easy to obtain.
* All moves can [[Instinct/Break|break Instinct]].
* Decent for PvP.

|'''[Z] Razor Wind'''
* Decent damage if held.
* Great stun.
* Has good follow-up combo potential.

|'''[X] Tornado Assault'''
* Somewhat decent combo potential.
* Decent stun.
* Direction where the target gets knocked into can be manipulated by turning the camera to where the user would want to get them launched (they still will go up), however, it is inconsistent.

|'''[C] Air Slasher'''
* Decent knockback.
* Good range.
* Good damage if all slashes hit.
* Has aim-assist.

|'''[F] Helicopter Flight'''
* Good pace of flight. (For a {{Common}} fruit)
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Lack of range.
* Low damage.
* Even though [[Rocket]] is less rare, it is still superior in terms of damage and grinding.
* Higher mastery requirement than [[Blade]] and [[Rocket]].

|'''[Z] Razor Wind'''
* Short range.
* Can be punished if missed because of the end lag.

|'''[X] Tornado Assault'''
* Very low damage if the full attack does not hit.
* Hard to control.
* Knocks up the target into the air makes it hard to land combos.

|'''[C] Air Slasher'''
* Can be punished if missed.
* Difficult to land all slashes in PvP.

|'''[F] Helicopter Flight'''
* Not fast enough to be viable in [[PvP]] or travel.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Spin’s fruit shape is based on a twisted prism, a geometric design that helps reduce wind resistance.
* Spin, along with [[Rocket]], are the only fruits to always be in Stock.
* Spin's pre-rework variant is used by the [[Marine Rear Admiral]]s at the [[Great Tree]] in the [[Third Sea]].
* Spin's {{Ability|X}} is similar to [[Shark Saw]]´s {{Ability|Shark Saw|X}}.

